  "notes": "Official 2024-2025 BCCC catalog program page (\"Program: Health Information Technology, AAS\", printed Program Total 64). Catalog lists a Prerequisites phase (18 credits) plus the sequenced plan (46 credits); both are included and reconcile to the printed 64. 0-credit Biology Placement Exam (test out of BIO 101) documented here only, not in external_prereqs. Accredited by the Commission on Accreditation for Health Informatics and Information Management Education (CAHIIM); MHEC-approved online program; graduates eligible for the RHIT national certification exam (AHIMA). Selective admission: complete application required (see bccc.edu/hit); minimum 2.5 GPA to apply, maintain 2.0; C or better in BIO 202/BIO 203 and all AHP and HIT courses; transfer/returning students may be required to repeat any AHP/HIT course whose credits are more than three years old. Students who wish to receive the Coding Specialist Certificate must take HIT 227 Advanced Medical Coding (already in the sequence). [Coordinator correction 2026-10-01: total_credits set to 46 (= sum of sequenced course credits) per corpus convention (external_prereqs excluded from the sum; cf. ABAC plans); collector had recorded 64 including the prerequisite phase. The catalog's printed program total and the prerequisite phase remain documented above.]",
